{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mr6bu1tyaaa","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"daemon cpu hot loop write path starvation root cause and fix","summary":"The :8787 daemon pegging to 100-140% CPU and starving its WRITE path (POST /overlay/note 5-20s+, /state 30s timeouts while GETs served slowly) was NOT the drain lanes retrying, git snapshots, or the .git/GRAPH_CHECKPOINT touch error (that touch error is a benign worktree-commit hook artifact, harmless). A v8-inspector CPU profile (kill -USR1 <pid>, hand-rolled WS client to Profiler.start, 12k samples) traced the burn to buildGraph -> projectGraphFromNative, which loops every native task (~1268) and per task ran THREE whole-graph scans: judge.judgingState/unverifiedEdgesForNode scanned all overlay.edges (~5333) = O(tasks x edges) ~6.7M comparisons/build; depRefs did overlay.edges.filter(e=>e.to===key) per task (same class); harnessTranscriptForTask re-scanned all agents + re-Date.parse'd bounds per task. Each uncached build blocked the event loop for many seconds; any write bumps the overlay mtime, invalidating the snapshot cache so every /state/session/task re-ran the quadratic build -\n\n[Long raw evidence preserved as structured source chunks.]","category":null,"tags":[],"created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-07-04T12:16:48.070Z","vec":[-0.03089730069041252,-0.0036554241087287664,-0.005465530790388584,0.0407479926943779,0.08080130070447922,-0.14855524897575378,-0.04761549085378647,0.03914478048682213,-0.010873976163566113,0.06437227129936218,-0.028091687709093094,0.025339510291814804,0.02059069089591503,-0.035182878375053406,-0.053950488567352295,-0.047194041311740875,0.05192942172288895,-0.03543508052825928,-0.003399268724024296,-0.03816800191998482,-0.041986387223005295,-0.008695154450833797,-0.005088245030492544,0.06370365619659424,0.04036829620599747,0.03537760674953461,-0.08423930406570435,-0.07246886938810349,-0.023557523265480995,-0.01007221918553114,-0.006944602355360985,0.00426207343116402